The implementation of the evaluator will depend upon the @newterm{syntax} of
the expressions to be evaluated being pinned down once, in a parser.  The
parser takes the data the given-code reader produces and maps each datum onto a
typed node: an assignment is represented directly as a @code{GSet} value
whose fields are the variable and the value expression.
Implementation of expressions will be described in
detail in @ref{4.1.2}.  There are also operations,
described in @ref{4.1.3}, that specify the representation of procedures
and environments.  For example, @code{GClosV} constructs compound
procedures, @code{GFrame.lookup} accesses the values of variables, and
the primitive table applies a primitive to a given list of arguments.

