be a Boolean expression, a chain nests them, and they short-circuit where the
source says they do --- the right operand of @code{&&} is evaluated only when
the left is true, and the right operand of @code{||} only when the left is
false.  Left to right, no operand evaluated after the decisive one: that
evaluation rule is the whole content of the forms, and the evaluator must
reproduce it exactly.

Define appropriate translation and evaluation procedures for the operators,
either as dedicated nodes of the sealed family or as derived expressions over
@code{GIf} --- which is how the translation of @ref{4.1.2} already rewrites
them.  Which of the two designs do you prefer, and why?
@end quotation

@quotation
@strong{@anchor{Exercise 4.5}Exercise 4.5:} The case analysis of
@ref{4.1.2} allows an additional clause form, the @newterm{recipient}
