(@ref{1.2.2}) uses a local named function as its loop:

@example kotlin
fun fib(n: Long): Long @{
    fun loop(a: Long, b: Long, count: Long): Long =
        if (count == 0L) b else loop(a + b,
            a,
            count - 1L)
    return loop(1L, 0L, n)
@}

fun main() @{
    println(fib(6L))
@}
// => 8
@end example

Modify @code{letToCombination} of @ref{Exercise 4.6} to also support the
